          en: ["Correct.", "<b>Wrong:</b> size and direction are different things. High volatility says a big move is coming, not which way.", "<b>Wrong:</b> in these data all test targets lie inside the training range (0.18–1.71), so this explanation does not hold here. Trees being unable to extend beyond the training range is a general limitation that matters when the regime changes; but two scores do not show the cause of the gap by themselves. Possible reasons are the forest's step-like forecasts and its learning the noise; testing this requires measuring the errors inside and outside the range separately.", "Correct."]
